libgphoto2_port/vusb: answer GetPartialObject in the virtual camera

The virtual PTP camera of the `vusb` port driver (configure --enable-vusb)
answers GetObject but not GetPartialObject, so ptp2's read_file_func, and with
it gp_camera_file_read(), returns GP_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED on it. Framehive reads
camera files only through gp_camera_file_read(), in chunks from the offset a
metadata reader seeks to (ADR 0034 §3), and drives its `camera:` commands in CI
through this virtual camera. This patch adds GetPartialObject (0x101B) to the
generic operations, written like GetObject, so a read takes the same path as on
a real PTP camera.

It changes only the `vusb` driver, which Framehive installs outside the iolib
folder that the library loads by default. It is written to be offered upstream.

Applied by flake.nix to nixpkgs' libgphoto2.

